fix(adapters): one HTTP-status classifier — a 429 was reported as a network fault

`code` is policy, not a label: `rate_limit` starts a PERSISTED platform cool-down
(batchSync → noteRateLimit) and replaces the adapter's message with a hardcoded
wait; `not_found` makes a history dig write `__END__`, permanently stopping that
channel from digging. Every other code changes only the wording.

Each adapter therefore classified HTTP status its own way, and they disagreed:

  weibo        403 → auth, everything else (INCLUDING 429) → network
  xiaohongshu  every status → network
  pixiv/fantia threw the status into a message; the outer catch made it network

So a platform answering `429 Too Many Requests` — the one response rule 19 exists
for — was reported as a connection problem and never entered a cool-down. We kept
requesting at full speed while the platform was asking us to stop.

`httpStatusError(status, platform)` is now the single mapping: `429 → rate_limit`,
`401/403 → auth`, `404/410 → not_found`, other `4xx → network`, `5xx → network`.
`404/410` is deliberately NOT used for an empty page: a transport-level 404 is
evidence about the request, not proof a channel is exhausted, and `not_found`
reaches `statesEndOfHistory`.

Adapters that wrap a whole try around acquisition can only classify in that catch,
where no status is visible — which is why pixiv/fantia flattened it. They now throw
`HttpStatusError`, and `toFetchError(err, platform, fallback)` takes the class from
the status while keeping the adapter's own message. A plain throw means the response
did not match the parser (`parse`), which is the other half of the queue entry:
a missing or renamed field is a schema change, not a network fault.

Also #15, same rule-1 category one layer down: `toSecureMediaUrl` decided where an
image is fetched from with `includes(...)`. Measured before the fix — all three
rewritten onto the platform CDN:

  https://evil.example/avatar/xhscdn.com.jpg   (domain in the path)
  https://xhscdn.com.attacker.tld/avatar/abc   (domain as a label prefix)
  https://notxhscdn.com/avatar/abc             (suffix spoof)

Now matched on the parsed hostname, and the three domains — which were written out
in `media.ts` AND in `proxyImage.ts` — live once in `hosts.ts` (`XHS_MEDIA_HOSTS`,
a subset of `PLATFORM_HOSTS`, asserted).

